  "policyUpdated": "Updated and effective: September 7, 2026",
  "privacyIntro": "This policy covers the current CantaVue app beta and this official website. Contact the CantaVue project at info@cantavue.com for privacy questions and requests. Features vary by platform and build; describing a feature here does not make it available.",
  "privacy1Title": "Local scores and practice data",
  "privacy1Body": "PDFs, images, score metadata, annotations, bookmarks, setlists, recordings, practice records and preferences that you import or create are primarily processed and saved in app storage on your device for reading, editing, playback and recovery. Core local features require no account. The current main app has no operational cloud account or automatic cloud upload; local preparation in Data and Sync does not mean data has been uploaded. This website cannot read your local score library.",
  "privacy2Title": "Camera, microphone and permissions",
  "privacy2Body": "The camera is used when you photograph or scan scores, or explicitly enable face gesture page turning. Score photos may remain temporarily in app cache and become a private PDF when saved to the library. Face gesture analysis happens on your device. It does not save or upload camera frames, face identifiers, facial landmarks or biometric templates, and is not used to identify a person.\n\nThe microphone supports recordings or local pitch tools that you start. Saved recordings stay locally; pitch analysis does not automatically upload audio. File and photo pickers process content you select. Notifications support enabled local practice reminders; local network access supports nearby sessions you start or join. Revoke permissions in system settings to stop or disable the related optional feature. Core local score reading does not require these permissions.",
  "privacy3Title": "Online scores and third-party websites",
  "privacy3Body": "When you choose online score search, search terms and selected work or download requests are sent to IMSLP and related content servers. They receive connection information such as your IP address. Their confirmation pages, cookies and sign-in flows are governed by their policies. The current download flow does not upload your private library. Cloud file providers and sharing destinations process data when you choose them through system file or share controls.",
  "privacy4Title": "Nearby devices and sharing",
  "privacy4Body": "When you enable CantaLink page following or remote control, connected devices exchange session authentication data, score and page-layout hashes, page positions or page-turn commands. The current nearby protocol does not send PDF contents, titles, annotations, recordings or accounts. Use trusted networks and share session links only with trusted participants. Exported or shared files go to the app, location or recipient you choose; deleting a local file does not recall shared copies.",
  "privacy5Title": "Website traffic, cookies and statistics",
  "privacy5Body": "OpenAI Sites hosts this website. To deliver pages, maintain security and produce basic traffic statistics, the hosting service processes request and technical information such as IP addresses, browser information, request times and visited paths. Sites provides visitor and page-view counts. We have not added advertising, cross-site tracking or third-party behavioral analytics SDKs to this website or the current app.\n\nThis website has no account registration, subscription or file-upload forms. Fonts and images are served with the site. Hosting may use necessary cookies or similar technologies. Third-party sites manage their own cookies; you can manage cookies through your browser. See the provider policies below for their data practices.",
  "privacy6Title": "Email feedback and TestFlight",
  "privacy6Body": "When you email us, we receive your email address, message and any screenshots, files or device details you choose to attach, to respond, investigate issues and improve the product. Share only what is needed and remove private scores, student identities and other sensitive content first. We do not automatically attach your library.\n\nWhen you install, use or submit feedback through TestFlight, Apple may provide developers with testing usage, crash and submitted feedback information. The details depend on the invitation method, your actions and Apple’s policy. This is separate from the app’s local data processing.",
  "privacy7Title": "Retention, deletion and backups",
  "privacy7Body": "Local data remains until you delete or clean it up. Moving scores to Recently Deleted does not immediately erase them permanently. Annotation history, local automatic snapshots and exported backups may retain older data; manage those copies separately. Uninstalling usually removes local app data, but does not automatically erase system backups, cloud files or exports.\n\nWe retain email and necessary issue records only for as long as needed to address and follow up on the issue or meet applicable obligations. Request deletion of information we hold at our feedback email. We cannot remotely delete a library stored only on your device. Apple, hosting and email providers manage their records under their policies.",
  "privacy8Title": "Providers, purposes and security",
  "privacy8Body": "Hosting and email providers process necessary information to deliver the website and support, and may process it outside your country or region. We do not sell personal information or use private scores or recordings for advertising or AI training. Where disclosure is legally required, we limit it to what is necessary.\n\nWe take reasonable measures to protect information we control and limit unrelated access, but cannot guarantee absolute storage or transmission security. Protect your device, email and backups, and do not publish nearby session links.",
  "privacy9Title": "Your choices and requests",
  "privacy9Body": "You can stop optional online features, revoke device permissions, and export or delete local content. Contact info@cantavue.com to ask whether we hold feedback information about you or to request access, correction, deletion or restriction under applicable law. We may reasonably verify the source of a request to avoid affecting someone else’s data. We handle requests under applicable law; this policy does not limit statutory complaint or other rights.",
  "privacy10Title": "Minors, changes and contact",
  "privacy10Body": "The current beta has no child accounts or school student-roster service. Minors should use optional online and feedback features with a guardian’s guidance. Teachers should not email identifiable student information. Contact us if a minor’s information has been provided inappropriately so it can be removed.\n\nWe will update this policy and effective date when features, providers or data practices change, and provide notice or seek consent where required. Privacy and support contact: info@cantavue.com.",
  "privacySources": "Related provider policies",
  "providerOpenAI": "OpenAI privacy policy",
  "providerApple": "Apple TestFlight & privacy",
  "providerImslp": "IMSLP privacy policy",
  "termsIntro": "These terms describe the use of the CantaVue website and current app beta. Contact the CantaVue project at info@cantavue.com. Installation and testing also follow the distribution platform’s applicable agreements; this page does not replace Apple’s standard license agreement.",
  "terms1Title": "Beta status and scope",
  "terms1Body": "The beta is for evaluation, testing and feedback. Features may change, stop working or contain errors. Website scenario images are labeled illustrations, not hardware certification, customer endorsements or guarantees of unreleased features. Public beta availability depends on an active official invitation and platform status.",
  "terms2Title": "Your scores and content rights",
  "terms2Body": "You retain rights you hold in scores, annotations, recordings and other content. Import, record, download or share only material you have permission to use, including any required permission for other people’s recordings or personal information. Using the app grants no rights to third-party scores; public availability does not establish permission in every region. Do not use the service to infringe rights, distribute unlawful content or interfere with others.",
  "terms3Title": "Saving, backups and performances",
  "terms3Body": "Keep original scores and independent exports or backups of important annotations and practice data. Sync preparation, local saving and external backup are distinct states. Test performance workflows and accessory compatibility beforehand and keep an appropriate fallback for reading scores. Beta defects may cause interruptions or data loss.",
  "terms4Title": "Third-party services and devices",
  "terms4Body": "Online score sources, system cloud file providers, TestFlight and other third-party services have their own providers, terms, copyright restrictions and availability. Camera, stylus, MIDI and pedal features depend on the platform, permissions and hardware. Scenario images do not establish compatibility with every model.",
  "terms5Title": "Charges, licenses and feedback",
  "terms5Body": "The current beta has no in-app purchase flow. Future release pricing or paid features will be described separately; sending feedback does not start a subscription. CantaVue-owned app, website and brand materials are protected by applicable rights; third-party and open-source materials retain their own licenses. We may use voluntarily submitted suggestions to improve the product without taking ownership of private scores, recordings or attachments.",
  "terms6Title": "Responsibility, statutory rights and changes",
  "terms6Body": "We provide the beta in its current state without promising uninterrupted, error-free use or suitability for every device or situation. Any limitation applies only where permitted by law and does not exclude non-excludable liability or consumer rights. Material changes will update this page’s date and be notified as required. Contact info@cantavue.com with questions.",
  "supportIntro": "Email info@cantavue.com for help, suggestions or privacy requests. Your own mail app sends the message; this page does not automatically upload information.",
  "supportEmailAction": "Email feedback",
  "support1Title": "Help us reproduce the issue",
  "support1Body": "Include your device model, OS version, app version and build number, steps, expected result and actual result. Redacted screenshots can help. Do not send passwords, session links, private scores or student information. TestFlight testers can also use the feedback option in TestFlight.",
  "support2Title": "Get started",
  "support2Body": "In the app, choose Create from template → Staff paper, enter a title and create a score to try reading and annotations without an account or private file. You can also import an authorized PDF through the system Files picker.",
  "support3Title": "Save and recover",
  "support3Body": "Wait for saving to finish, return to the library and reopen the score to confirm your annotations. Export important scores and complete backups before beta updates. Try recovery with test data first. If something goes wrong, preserve original files and backups instead of repeatedly overwriting them.",
  "support4Title": "Permissions and beta access",
  "support4Body": "Photography, recording, pitch tools, nearby sessions and reminders need permissions only when you choose those features; manage them in system settings. iOS and iPadOS testing uses TestFlight, with installation subject to review and invitation status. We will update the website when a public invitation is available.",
  "feedbackEmail": "info@cantavue.com"
